            <ArticleTitle>Why pick on propoxyphene? The evidence demands it.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While propoxyphene may have filled a niche when it was first marketed in 1957, newer, safer agents are now available. Multiple experts list the drug as one to avoid in the elderly patient. Evidence-based practice requires its use be minimized, especially in individuals over the age of 65.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
